  "id": "COMPOUND:3624 - PROTEIN:1477",
  "verbalization": "Cadaverine is implicated in the relationship with the Sodium- and chloride-dependent GABA transporter 1 through a multi-step pathway involving different molecular targets. The evidence suggests that Cadaverine acts as a target for multiple entities, with the Sodium channel subunit beta-2 serving as a common intermediate in several pathways. This subunit is targeted by Npc11947, which in turn targets the GABA transporter 1. Similarly, Cadaverine is also linked to Potassium channel subfamily K member 3, which is targeted by Benzofuran-6-carbaldehyde, also targeting the GABA transporter 1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Cadaverine may influence the function of these channels and transporters through indirect interactions, possibly by modulating the activity of the intermediate targets. The presence of multiple distinct targets for Cadaverine, each leading to the GABA transporter 1, suggests a complex regulatory network that may involve different molecular mechanisms, yet all converge on the same final target.",
